Method:
We will start with a character-level N-gram model (likely 3 or 5-gram) using python and standard frameworks like pytorch, numpy, and matplotlib. N-gram models have very fast inference, which will help with the processing time metric, and are fairly easy to implement so this seems like a decent place to start. One concern is that N-gram models will not capture context beyond the N characters, so in the future we might fine-tune an open-source Transformer model for primary predictions then use a N-gram model for fast fallback predictions. 

